  "id": "COMPOUND:32420 - PROTEIN:1105",
  "verbalization": "Oblonganoside C appears to interact with the Gamma-aminobutyric acid receptor subunit beta-2 through a series of molecular pathways, with flavopiridol acting as a common target in all three paths. The evidence suggests that Oblonganoside C may modulate the activity of LIM domain kinase 2 or Cytochrome P450 2E1, which in turn influence the Gamma-aminobutyric acid receptor subunit beta-2. This indicates a potential regulatory mechanism where Oblonganoside C could either directly or indirectly affect the receptor through these intermediate targets. The presence of a shared target, flavopiridol, further supports a possible functional link between Oblonganoside C and the receptor, though the exact nature of the interaction remains unclear. The integration of these pathways highlights the complexity of the molecular network involved, emphasizing the role of flavopiridol as a central mediator in the observed effects.",
